ROLE: product-designer
STATUS: reviewed, corrected, browser-verified

ARTIFACTS:
- docs/prototype/openclaw-auto-marketing-hub-full-v13-gpt-codex.html
- docs/WIREFRAMES/openclaw-auto-marketing-hub-full-v13-gpt-codex.md

REVIEW OUTCOME:
- Existing v13 had MAJOR gaps: 25 route types were not all reachable, text8 used Bluesky instead of LINE, video3 incorrectly exposed Publish, current 224px shell/native preview treatment was replaced by a generic 244px card grid, Settings had 6 non-current tabs, and repair implied another publish.
- Corrected text8 to Threads, X, Facebook, Instagram, Telegram, Discord, Slack, LINE.
- Corrected video3 to YouTube Shorts, Instagram Reels, TikTok with `원고 저장` and `영상 작업실로` only. Studio video Publish controls = 0 and legacy bulk remains direct4 only.
- Added safe recovery: confirmed pre-send failure retries one card; uncertain checks existing provider result; published with missing local record repairs without republishing.
- Added Settings customer8 tabs, provider account confirmation, provider-specific tab sets, shared MH-2048 Inbox/Calendar reference, and all disabled/external/operator/services/legal terminal views.

OFFICIAL BENCHMARKS:
- Buffer scheduling: one composer can preview per channel and separates Now from scheduling choices. Borrowed channel-specific output and immediate/scheduled separation; retained Marketing Hub's current Studio shell and direct4 boundary.
  https://support.buffer.com/article/642-scheduling-posts
- Later Social Sets: profiles are grouped by brand or identity, and wrong-profile recovery recommends confirming the intended login. Borrowed visible account identity and explicit account confirmation; did not copy Later's plan model.
  https://help.later.com/hc/en-us/articles/360044369654-Create-Manage-Social-Sets
- Hootsuite calendar: calendar actions remain attached to content status. Borrowed the shared job reference between Studio, Inbox, and Calendar; retained current queue ownership labels.
  https://help.hootsuite.com/s/article/manage-content-calendar?language=en_US

BROWSER EVIDENCE, ACTUAL TOOL OUTPUT:
- 1440x1000: `{navDesktop:26, routeViews:25, cards:11, videoPublish:0, overflow:0, targets:0}`; console errors 0.
- 1024x900: `{navDesktop:26, routeViews:25, cards:11, videoPublish:0, overflow:0, targets:0}`; console errors 0.
- 390x844 Studio with open alternate navigation: `{navDesktop:26, routeViews:25, cards:11, videoPublish:0, overflow:0, targets:0, mobileNav:26}`; console errors 0.
- 390 route loop: all 25 entries returned non-empty views, overflow 0, targets below 44px 0.
- Core recovery clicks: Facebook failed confirmed to published with retry permalink; Instagram uncertain to published with no-new-post confirmation permalink; Telegram repair required to published with recovered record permalink. Video Publish count stayed 0.
- Schedule click loop: create to change retained MH-2048, cancel returned schedule null.
- JavaScript parse: `JS_OK`; `git diff --check` passed for the two allowed artifacts.

RED TEAM:
- Attack: placing Publish on video3 turns a hand-off into an unsupported success promise and creates a second video delivery state machine inside Studio.
- Revision: video3 was removed from per-card and bulk publish branches. Each video card can save its script and open `/videos`, while text8 retains card actions according to capability.

SELF-INTERROGATION:
- If this review is wrong, the most likely reason is conflating 26 sidebar destinations with 25 route types. The prototype now holds separate manifests and the browser measured `navDesktop=26`, `mobileNav=26`, and `routeViews=25` independently.
- A second load-bearing risk was hiding overflow with CSS. The route loop measured `scrollWidth-clientWidth=0` after rendering every route at 390, and each visible interactive target measured at least 44px.

DESIGN REVIEW:
- Design Score: B+
- Current visual-system continuity: B+
- Workflow truthfulness and recovery: A
- Responsive navigation and accessibility: A
- Provider capability differentiation: A
- Pixel fidelity to every current product route: B

LIMITS / 회수 필요:
- 회수 필요: provider adapter, job ledger, idempotency, account schema, and real permalink readback remain eng-design decisions. The prototype does not claim external execution.
- Hootsuite help content loaded only its official shell because the site returned a client-side CSS gate; its role is limited to the official URL already pinned by the approved PRD.

